\title{A generalized Blakers–Massey theorem}
\author{mathieuanel}
\author{georgbiedermann}
\author{ericfinster}
\author{andrejoyal}
\tag{hott}
\meta{doi}{10.1112/topo.12163}
\meta{venue}{[[jtopol]] 13(4)}
\taxon{Reference}
\date{2020-09-07}

\subtree{
\taxon{Abstract}

\p{
We prove a generalization of the classical connectivity theorem of Blakers–Massey,
valid in an arbitrary higher topos and with respect to an arbitrary modality, that
is, a factorization system #{(L,R)} in which the left class is stable by base change.
We explain how to rederive the classical result, as well as a recent generalization
by Chachólski–Scherer–Werndli. Our proof is inspired by the one given in Homotopy
Type Theory.
}
}

